From be3d7fa462829af675b7b1bc56a429cb055f24cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiwaz <82827604+TiwazM@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:26:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] MEGA65: uartmon commands for automated testing: ~frames
 ~joy ~shot ~sleepless ~mem

Lets a test harness or an AI agent drive the emulator through the
existing UART monitor socket with frame-exact control:

  ~frames N      run exactly N (hex) frames, then pause and show registers
  ~joy1/2 XX     hold joystick bits (1 up 2 down 4 left 8 right 10 fire)
  ~shot PATH     write the next completed frame as PNG to PATH
  ~sleepless 0/1 real-time pacing off/on
  ~mem ADDR LEN  one-line hex dump of up to $20000 bytes (28-bit address)

The joystick mask is ANDed into the CIA1 reads so a host joystick keeps
working. The write buffer grows to 256 KB for ~mem and answers are
flushed as long as the socket accepts them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 targets/mega65/input_devices.c |  5 +-
 targets/mega65/mega65.c        |  3 ++
 targets/mega65/uart_monitor.c  | 98 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 targets/mega65/uart_monitor.h  |  4 ++
 targets/mega65/vic4.c          |  6 ++-
 5 files changed, 111 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

